{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/hate-speech",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "hate speech"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Disparaging expressions directed at individuals or groups based on specific social characteristics, which can take many forms – written, non-verbal, visual, artistic, etc. – while being disseminated through any medium, including the Internet, print materials, radio, or television."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "Hate speech not only undermines the dignity of the individuals and groups targeted but also violates the fundamental principles of peaceful coexistence and mutual respect that underpin democratic societies. Its negative effects extend beyond the social and personal spheres, having a troubling impact on the language-learning process. The consequences of hate speech are multifaceted and far-reaching. Research has shown that hate speech has significant psychological and emotional consequences for victims, affecting their self-esteem, self-perception, and interactions with their environment."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "13.7.2"
  ],
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/hate",
    "prefLabel": {
